# 0.5: the `(lines A–B)` range inside the operand-contiguity
# diagnostic is re-based to FILE line numbers, like the `Line N:` prefix it
# sits behind.
#
# The prefix was always re-based per section; the range quoted inside the
# message was computed from section-local rows and was not, so in a document
# whose sequence section is not the first the two numbers disagreed. Here the
# message reported `Line 21` with `(lines 6–8)`, a range that points into this
# comment. The operand's members are on lines 20 and 22, and the split run is
# 20–22.
figdown 0.5 block
node a "A"
node b "B"

figdown 0.5 sequence
lifeline c "Client"
lifeline s "Server"
fragment f "optional" type=opt
operand o "guard" in=f
message c -> s "one" in=o
message c -> s "splits the run"
message c -> s "two" in=o
